# November 19, 2026: St. Augustine and Anastasia Island, St. Johns County, Florida. Region drawn at random by
# tools/choose.py (fl). The old Spanish city: its coquina fort and watchtower, the shell-rock quarries they were cut from,
# colonial houses, churches and burying grounds, and Flagler's poured-concrete hotels of the 1880s.
# Sources read in this session: Wikipedia articles (tools/wiki_raw.py), National Register nomination forms (NPGallery
# "_text" PDFs read with tools/page.py), National Park Service hours and directions pages, the Florida State Parks
# brochure for Anastasia State Park, HMdb marker pages, and the managing bodies' own pages where they opened. Where a
# managing body's page refused the tool (the St. Augustine Historical Society, the Ximenez-Fatio House, Florida State
# Parks' web pages), hours are taken from the St. Johns County visitor bureau's listing (visitstaugustine.com) and the
# access note says so. Interiors were not visited by any source opened unless the entry says so.
